===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[fall away]] gradually; to [[subside]].
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To fall into [[error]] or [[heresy]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Cymbeline|act=III|scene=vi|page=385|column=2|passage=To '''lapſe''' in Fullneſſe / Is ſorer, than to lye for Neede: and Falſhood / Is worſe in Kings, than Beggers.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To slip into a bad habit that one is trying to avoid.
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To become [[void]].
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To fall or pass from one proprietor to another, or from the original destination, by the omission, negligence, or failure of somebody, such as a [[patron]] or [[legatee]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1726|author=John Ayliffe|title=Parergon Juris Canonici Anglicani|location=London|publisher=Printed for the Author by D. Leach|oclc=6977383|page=116|passage=...and if the archbishop shall not fill it up within six Months ensuing, it '''lapses''' to the King, but according to the ''Canon'' Law to the Pope.}}

